# A token copy of Summon: Esper Maduin (Three Steps Ahead's "+ {3} - Create a token that's a copy of target artifact or
# creature you control"). The original is the back face of Esper Origins, so the copy is a double-faced token that enters
# with that face up (CR 707.8a; the Esper Origins ruling): a 4/4 green Saga Elemental. It enters with the lore counter
# every Saga enters with (CR 714.3a), which triggers its own chapter I - the top card, Ornithopter, is revealed and put into
# the hand - but not with a finality counter: counters are not copied (CR 707.2), and only the original was put onto the
# battlefield "with a finality counter on it". The original by then has two lore counters (its chapter II on turn 3).

